{"step_index":92,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:59:05Z","thinking":"**Generating Document Components**\n\nI've successfully generated all the four-word `.docx` and `.txt` documents. These include high-contrast, centered images within the Word docs specifically for the Assertion-Reason questions and the case studies.  These files now have 100% NC.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Updated walkthrough showing embedded images in Case Studies and Assertion-Reason questions, and full verification of the NCERT rationalized syllabus (removal of tangents/normals).","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Half-Yearly Examination 2026–27: Class XII Mathematics\n## Final Walkthrough & Updated Delivery\n\n### Summary of Completed Files\nAll Question Papers and Marking Schemes have been updated with **high-contrast embedded diagrams** for all Case-Based and Assertion–Reason questions, and **100% rationalized NCERT syllabus compliance** (removing all deleted topics including Tangents & Normals).\n\n#### File Locations\nDirectory: `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\`\n\n1. **Set A Question Paper**\n   - Word Document: [Set_A_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.docx)\n   - Text Source: [Set_A_Question_Paper.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.txt)\n\n2. **Set A Marking Scheme & Step-by-Step Solutions**\n   - Word Document: [Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx)\n   - Text Source: [Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt)\n\n3. **Set B Question Paper**\n   - Word Document: [Set_B_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.docx)\n   - Text Source: [Set_B_Question_Paper.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.txt)\n\n4. **Set B Marking Scheme & Step-by-Step Solutions**\n   - Word Document: [Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx)\n   - Text Source: [Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt)\n\n---\n\n### Embedded High-Contrast Diagrams\n\n| Question | Diagram Included | Set A | Set B |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Q19 (AR)** | Visual graph showing continuity vs differentiability | $y = \\|x - 2\\|$ corner point | $y = [x]$ step discontinuities |\n| **Q20 (AR)** | Graph showing local extrema / monotonicity | $y = -(x-3)^2 + 4$ maximum at $(3,4)$ | $y = \\ln x$ strictly increasing curve |\n| **Q36 (Case 1)** | Relations & Functions diagram | Partition into Equivalence Classes | Directed Divisibility Relation Graph |\n| **Q37 (Case 2)** | Application of Derivatives diagram | Production Cost Curve $C(x)$ | Total Revenue Curve $R(x)$ |\n| **Q38 (Case 3)** | Integrals kinematics graph | Velocity–Time $v(t) = 3t^2 - 12t + 9$ | Velocity–Time $v(t) = 6t^2 - 4t$ |\n\n---\n\n### Deleted Syllabus Audit & Corrections\n\n1. **Tangents & Normals (Chapter 6):**\n   - *Audit finding:* Old CBSE syllabus had \"Tangents and Normals\" (Exercise 6.3) and \"Approximations\" (Exercise 6.4), which are deleted in the rationalized NCERT.\n   - *Corrections made:* Replaced all tangent/normal questions with in-syllabus NCERT problems:\n     - **Set A Q15:** Maximum value of $\\sin x + \\cos x$ on $[0, \\pi/2]$\n     - **Set A Q16:** Marginal revenue from total revenue function $R(x) = 3x^2 + 36x + 5$\n     - **Set A Q24:** Rate of increase of cube volume ($dV/dt$) given edge growth rate\n     - **Set B Q15:** Rate of change of sphere surface area ($dS/dr$)\n     - **Set B Q24:** Rate of change of circle area ($dA/dt$)\n2. **Inverse Trigonometric Functions (Chapter 2):** Only principal values and domains used; no deleted sum/difference formulas.\n3. **Relations and Functions (Chapter 1):** Zero composite/invertible functions or binary operations.\n4. **Matrices & Determinants (Chapters 3 & 4):** Zero elementary row transformations or determinant property proofs.\n5. **Calculus (Chapters 5 & 7):** Zero Rolle's/MVT or limit-of-a-sum questions.\n","Description":"Updated walkthrough showing complete image embeddings and rationalized syllabus audit.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b78a5d36-6586-4c94-a487-70da0c9f5362\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Updating walkthrough","toolSummary":"Update walkthrough artifact"}}]}
